<p class="lt-chem-134629">To easily see the <em><strong>range </strong></em>and <em><strong>median </strong></em>it is convenient to arrange the data in terms of increasing or decreasing values. Thus: 0.3779, 0.3784, 0.3791, 0.3793, and 0.3797 g. Since this data set has an odd number of trials, the <em><strong>median </strong></em>is simply the middle datum or 3<sup>rd</sup> datum, 0.3791 g. Note that for a finite data set the <em><strong>median </strong></em>and<em><strong>mean</strong></em><em><strong> </strong></em>are not necessarily identical. The <em><strong>range </strong></em>is 0.3797 &ndash; 0.3779 g or 0.0018.</p>

